1
00:00:07,089 --> 00:00:08,799
Golf. I don't get it.

2
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:10,968
Pointless, absurd,
repetitive activity...

3
00:00:11,093 --> 00:00:12,553
Very good for clearing the mind.

4
00:00:12,678 --> 00:00:15,765
All these stalls here?
Mental washing machines.

5
00:00:16,182 --> 00:00:17,725
Van Pelt, what do we got?

6
00:00:18,184 --> 00:00:20,728
According to his driver's license,
this is Micah Newton.

7
00:00:20,895 --> 00:00:22,730
Murder weapon appears to be
the 5-iron there.

8
00:00:23,314 --> 00:00:25,316
- No defense wounds.
- Or witnesses.

9
00:00:25,525 --> 00:00:27,860
Coroner thinks he was struck
from behind while hitting balls.

10
00:00:28,361 --> 00:00:31,197
Sunblock, hand sanitizer,
healthy snacks.

11
00:00:31,364 --> 00:00:33,324
Somebody grew up
with a protective mother.

12
00:00:33,699 --> 00:00:36,118
Another golfer found him
around 4:00 this morning.

13
00:00:36,410 --> 00:00:38,871
Killer left the victim's golf bag
and wallet intact.

14
00:00:39,080 --> 00:00:40,414
Cho's going through
the car now.

15
00:00:40,790 --> 00:00:42,041
It's pretty early to go golfing.

16
00:00:42,416 --> 00:00:44,418
Apparently 4:00 a.m. is the beginning
of the morning rush.

17
00:00:44,710 --> 00:00:46,003
Place runs 24 hours a day.

18
00:00:46,254 --> 00:00:47,380
Talk to the management
and have them give you

19
00:00:47,505 --> 00:00:49,048
all the security footage
from last night.

20
00:00:49,298 --> 00:00:50,341
Yes, boss.

21
00:00:50,466 --> 00:00:52,843
- Jane, focus.
- Trying. There it is.

22
00:00:53,261 --> 00:00:54,554
Very hard
to find the correct knob.

23
00:00:54,762 --> 00:00:56,597
- On the victim.
- Ah. Sorry.

24
00:00:56,722 --> 00:01:00,142
Yes, uh, he is a professional,
health-conscious.

25
00:01:00,393 --> 00:01:04,021
When you factor in the specially
monogrammed windbreaker

26
00:01:04,146 --> 00:01:07,191
and the iodine stains
under the fingernails

27
00:01:07,984 --> 00:01:10,236
and the illegible scroll
on these scorecards

28
00:01:10,903 --> 00:01:14,156
you can only draw one conclusion
our man here was a doctor.

29
00:01:14,574 --> 00:01:16,033
Somehow that makes sense.

30
00:01:17,118 --> 00:01:19,620
- A doctor with a problem.
- What kind of problem?

31
00:01:19,787 --> 00:01:22,957
This impact label
was marking his shots.

32
00:01:23,249 --> 00:01:27,378
And in this particular case,
the "x" doesn't mark the spot.

33
00:01:28,254 --> 00:01:30,381
His shots are more
at the front of the club.

34
00:01:30,673 --> 00:01:32,300
- What does that mean?
- Well, it means that he was...

35
00:01:32,425 --> 00:01:35,678
"Slicing them.
Coming across the face."

36
00:01:36,887 --> 00:01:38,347
Happens when you're
feeling stressed.

37
00:01:38,931 --> 00:01:40,766
Lisbon, may I speak
with you?

38
00:01:41,559 --> 00:01:43,102
We really need
to get you a bell.

39
00:01:45,688 --> 00:01:49,900
I wonder, have you developed any theories
on where agent Hightower might be?

40
00:01:50,359 --> 00:01:51,402
No.

41
00:01:52,194 --> 00:01:53,863
Has she been
in contact with you?

42
00:01:55,197 --> 00:01:57,450
You mean, have I had contact
with a wanted felon

43
00:01:57,575 --> 00:02:00,911
without notifying my superiors?
No, I have not.

44
00:02:01,412 --> 00:02:04,206
You spent a day with
Hightower's children at CBI.

45
00:02:04,790 --> 00:02:05,833
What were they like?

46
00:02:06,667 --> 00:02:08,544
I'll get back to you on that.
Excuse me.

47
00:02:10,212 --> 00:02:11,339
Cho, what'd you find?

48
00:02:11,505 --> 00:02:13,090
Victim's I.D. Badge
was in his briefcase.

49
00:02:13,215 --> 00:02:14,925
He's a doctor
over at blessed sacrament.

50
00:02:15,176 --> 00:02:17,219
Oh! You may touch
the hem of my garment.

51
00:02:17,553 --> 00:02:19,513
- What's this attached to it?
- It's a radiation badge.

52
00:02:19,639 --> 00:02:22,808
Monitors exposure to hospital radiation.
I'll have the coroner's office test it

53
00:02:22,933 --> 00:02:24,018
when they do the autopsy.

54
00:02:24,727 --> 00:02:26,562
I wasn't finished, agent Lisbon.

55
00:02:26,937 --> 00:02:29,357
Agent Laroche, this is a crime scene.
I'm busy.

56
00:02:29,607 --> 00:02:33,194
Curious... your disinterest
in finding Hightower.

57
00:02:33,402 --> 00:02:34,445
Are you for real?

58
00:02:34,570 --> 00:02:36,697
We've had to endure
your surprise visits for months.

59
00:02:36,822 --> 00:02:38,741
You named your killer.
She's on the run.

60
00:02:38,949 --> 00:02:41,243
Why do you keep showing up
on my crime scenes?

61
00:02:41,494 --> 00:02:43,913
- Because this morning, I...
- I don't even want to hear it!

62
00:02:44,205 --> 00:02:45,998
The second Hightower's
replacement is announced

63
00:02:46,123 --> 00:02:48,709
I'm gonna put in a formal request
to keep you away from me.

64
00:02:50,127 --> 00:02:55,174
As I was saying, this morning I was
assigned to take over Hightower's duties.

65
00:02:55,466 --> 00:02:59,261
- Which include overseeing this team.
- Oops-a-daisy.

66
00:03:00,554 --> 00:03:03,724
I appreciate your candor
and I'm going to honor your request.

67
00:03:04,016 --> 00:03:06,018
- Agent Cho?
- Yeah?

68
00:03:06,310 --> 00:03:08,521
I'm putting you in charge of the team
as of right now.

69
00:03:09,105 --> 00:03:11,899
Agent Lisbon, you report to agent Cho.

70
00:03:13,442 --> 00:03:14,485
Good day...

71
00:03:38,090 --> 00:03:40,676
Hey. I talked to the team.
We figured it out.

72
00:03:40,801 --> 00:03:41,844
What's that?

73
00:03:41,969 --> 00:03:44,054
Well, you run the investigation.
Call the shots like usual.

74
00:03:44,179 --> 00:03:47,141
- I'll report to Laroche.
- I appreciate the offer, but no.

75
00:03:47,558 --> 00:03:51,186
- You're the boss. This isn't right.
- It's a direct order. You are in charge.

76
00:03:53,063 --> 00:03:54,606
If I'm in charge,
I have to be in charge for real.

77
00:03:54,773 --> 00:03:56,567
I will back you 100%.

78
00:03:56,734 --> 00:03:58,736
You're a senior agent.
Show 'em what you got.

79
00:03:59,653 --> 00:04:01,155
- You sure?
- I'm positive.

80
00:04:01,321 --> 00:04:03,031
I'll clear out my office for you
this afternoon.

81
00:04:03,240 --> 00:04:04,575
- I don't want your office.
- I told you, it's o...

82
00:04:04,700 --> 00:04:06,410
I prefer no walls between me
and my team.

83
00:04:10,205 --> 00:04:11,248
How'd it go?

84
00:04:11,915 --> 00:04:13,584
{\an8}- I'm in charge.
- Got it.

85
00:04:13,792 --> 00:04:15,586
{\an8}- Any orders, boss?
- No, really.

86
00:04:16,128 --> 00:04:17,588
{\an8}Lisbon didn't go for it.
I'm in charge.

87
00:04:19,757 --> 00:04:22,259
{\an8}Oh. Well, congratulations.

88
00:04:23,552 --> 00:04:24,595
Let's break down the case.

89
00:04:33,479 --> 00:04:36,106
All right. Lisbon, can you please fill in
the personal details you've learned?

90
00:04:36,315 --> 00:04:39,777
{\an8}Sure. Micah Newton, age 42.
He's survived by a husband.

91
00:04:39,902 --> 00:04:42,905
{\an8}He's an M.D. but he played mostly an
administrative role at the hospital.

92
00:04:43,155 --> 00:04:44,865
{\an8}And, Van Pelt, did you find anything
on the surveillance tapes

93
00:04:44,990 --> 00:04:46,033
{\an8}from the driving range?

94
00:04:46,158 --> 00:04:48,202
{\an8}No help. Cameras only cover
the parking lot and clubhouse.

95
00:04:48,368 --> 00:04:49,661
{\an8}Killer must have parked
on the street.

96
00:04:50,037 --> 00:04:51,705
{\an8}- Fingerprints on the club?
- None usable.

97
00:04:52,080 --> 00:04:54,625
- We have a coroner's report yet? Okay.
- Yeah. Right here.

98
00:04:58,420 --> 00:05:01,590
{\an8}The, uh, blow to the head
caused an instant cerebral hemorrhage.

99
00:05:01,715 --> 00:05:02,758
{\an8}No surprises there.

100
00:05:02,925 --> 00:05:04,885
But there were questions
about his radiation exposure.

101
00:05:05,052 --> 00:05:06,094
What kind of questions?

102
00:05:06,220 --> 00:05:09,139
Well, hospital personnel wear badges
to keep tabs on their radiation exposure.

103
00:05:09,431 --> 00:05:10,641
{\an8}Now according to Newton's badge

104
00:05:10,766 --> 00:05:12,017
{\an8}he was way over the limit
for this month.

105
00:05:12,434 --> 00:05:14,311
With levels like that, he should
have been glowing in the dark.

106
00:05:14,436 --> 00:05:17,147
{\an8}But the coroner's test of his body found it
within an acceptable range.

107
00:05:17,397 --> 00:05:18,440
How could that happen?

108
00:05:18,565 --> 00:05:19,858
{\an8}Lisbon, take Jane
to the hospital and find out.

109
00:05:20,025 --> 00:05:21,902
{\an8}- Yes, sir.
- I'll talk to the husband.

110
00:05:22,528 --> 00:05:24,780
{\an8}Van Pelt, check into Newton's records.
Rigsby, you're with me.

111
00:05:24,905 --> 00:05:25,948
{\an8}Okay.

112
00:05:31,870 --> 00:05:33,539
{\an8}You have a chance
to read the case files yet?

113
00:05:33,705 --> 00:05:36,542
{\an8}No need. I saw enough at the crime
scene to know that a doctor did it.

114
00:05:36,750 --> 00:05:37,793
{\an8}How can you tell?

115
00:05:37,918 --> 00:05:40,963
{\an8}A single blow to the head
causing instant death...

116
00:05:41,588 --> 00:05:45,759
{\an8}That takes medical know-how, a strong ego
and a killer golf swing.

117
00:05:45,926 --> 00:05:48,262
{\an8}Definitely a doctor-on-doctor crime.

118
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:49,930
Are you the CBI agents?

119
00:05:50,055 --> 00:05:53,183
{\an8}Yes, she does the detecting,
And I do the insulting.

120
00:05:53,308 --> 00:05:55,143
{\an8}- Consulting.
- That, too.

121
00:05:55,853 --> 00:05:58,438
Francine Trent.
I'm Dr. Newton's assistant...

122
00:05:59,106 --> 00:06:01,275
- Was, I guess.
- I'm sorry.

123
00:06:02,150 --> 00:06:03,193
If you'll follow me.

124
00:06:04,236 --> 00:06:06,530
{\an8}Here's Dr. Newton's schedule
from yesterday.

125
00:06:07,197 --> 00:06:08,240
Thank you.

126
00:06:09,908 --> 00:06:10,951
According to this

127
00:06:11,076 --> 00:06:13,453
the last appointment he had scheduled
to give a lecture at 8:00?

128
00:06:13,912 --> 00:06:16,915
To the first-year medical students.
It was a highlight of his year.

129
00:06:17,791 --> 00:06:20,210
I see you have the same
radiation badge he did.

130
00:06:20,752 --> 00:06:22,588
We're required to wear them
at all times.

131
00:06:22,838 --> 00:06:25,090
Any idea why his levels
were off the chart?

132
00:06:25,591 --> 00:06:32,973
No. Um, we use radioactive substances
like cesium-137 for blood irradiation

133
00:06:33,098 --> 00:06:38,061
but everybody wears lead shielding
so they're protected, so... I don't know.

134
00:06:38,520 --> 00:06:39,938
Did you get an invite
to the wedding?

135
00:06:40,522 --> 00:06:42,524
- I did.
- How was it?

136
00:06:42,941 --> 00:06:43,984
It was lovely.

137
00:06:47,070 --> 00:06:49,865
- Who are these people?
- Transplant patients.

138
00:06:50,282 --> 00:06:52,910
Dr. Newton started the transplant board
at blessed sacrament.

139
00:06:53,285 --> 00:06:54,786
Gave him tremendous joy.

140
00:06:55,078 --> 00:06:56,997
- Are they still alive?
- Jane...

141
00:06:57,164 --> 00:06:58,498
You're not my boss anymore.

142
00:06:59,499 --> 00:07:01,293
Transplants are a tricky business.

143
00:07:01,418 --> 00:07:03,587
But I-I've seen
so many people saved...

144
00:07:04,046 --> 00:07:05,130
People who were going to die.

145
00:07:05,297 --> 00:07:06,840
Yeah, well I'll let you in
on a little secret...

146
00:07:06,965 --> 00:07:08,800
- We're all gonna die.
- I am so sorry.

147
00:07:08,967 --> 00:07:10,010
That's okay.

148
00:07:10,135 --> 00:07:13,096
Being scared of doctors and hospitals
is perfectly normal.

149
00:07:13,263 --> 00:07:14,306
I'm not.

150
00:07:14,431 --> 00:07:18,518
Um, so, uh, did he actually
go to his lecture at 8:00?

151
00:07:18,727 --> 00:07:20,520
Yeah, he never missed
an opportunity

152
00:07:20,687 --> 00:07:22,940
to give a motivational speech
to young doctors.

153
00:07:23,607 --> 00:07:26,276
He was a good practitioner,
but a better leader.

154
00:07:27,235 --> 00:07:29,237
I think it's why he moved
into administration.

155
00:07:30,030 --> 00:07:31,531
And who's this rogue's gallery?

156
00:07:31,657 --> 00:07:33,659
All the physicians
on the transplant board.

157
00:07:33,867 --> 00:07:36,203
- Dr. Newton was chairman.
- Yet he stands to the side

158
00:07:36,328 --> 00:07:38,455
and this man takes center stage.
Who's he?

159
00:07:38,872 --> 00:07:41,124
Dr. Quick, chief of surgery.

160
00:07:41,583 --> 00:07:44,753
As of this morning, he took over
Dr. Newton's responsibilities.

161
00:07:45,253 --> 00:07:47,297
- Now we're getting somewhere.
- Can we speak to him?

162
00:07:47,589 --> 00:07:49,216
He's leading
the transplant board meeting.

163
00:07:49,424 --> 00:07:50,759
That's a fast transition.

164
00:07:50,968 --> 00:07:53,804
Dr. Quick said the meeting
was too important to postpone.

165
00:07:53,929 --> 00:07:55,973
- Will there be other doctors there?
- All of them.

166
00:07:56,807 --> 00:07:59,267
A roomful of doctors?
Manna from heaven.

167
00:07:59,434 --> 00:08:00,811
Could you please take us there?

168
00:08:02,020 --> 00:08:03,981
I'll be on my best behavior.
I won't say a word.

169
00:08:04,439 --> 00:08:06,650
Excuse me. David Vance,
event director?

170
00:08:06,942 --> 00:08:09,152
Uh, he's in the back.
I'll go get him.

171
00:08:09,361 --> 00:08:10,404
Thanks.

172
00:08:11,196 --> 00:08:13,740
{\an8}- So listen, delicate question.
- Yes?

173
00:08:14,032 --> 00:08:16,159
Thursday quiz night is strictly
no bosses, as you know.

174
00:08:16,493 --> 00:08:18,870
Should we give your spot
to Lisbon?

175
00:08:19,121 --> 00:08:21,373
- Feels kind of weird.
- Do what you feel is right.

176
00:08:21,498 --> 00:08:23,959
Or should we just hang on to your spot
in case you screw up?

177
00:08:25,419 --> 00:08:26,461
It's just a joke.

178
00:08:26,920 --> 00:08:27,963
Yeah. Funny.

179
00:08:28,922 --> 00:08:30,048
You're gonna make a hell
of a boss man.

180
00:08:30,215 --> 00:08:31,258
I'm already scared of you.

181
00:08:34,011 --> 00:08:35,220
Thank you
for meeting me here.

182
00:08:36,013 --> 00:08:38,181
I... I would have cancelled this gala

183
00:08:38,348 --> 00:08:41,435
but it's my charity's biggest fund-raising
opportunity of the year.

184
00:08:41,727 --> 00:08:43,186
When was the last time
you saw your husband?

185
00:08:43,729 --> 00:08:45,022
Yesterday morning.

186
00:08:46,231 --> 00:08:49,651
We're early risers.
Well, I'm the early riser.

187
00:08:50,986 --> 00:08:52,362
My work is about an hour
from home

188
00:08:52,487 --> 00:08:56,408
and Micah would just get up
to be with me...

189
00:08:57,951 --> 00:08:59,369
even after a 12-hour shift.

190
00:08:59,578 --> 00:09:01,163
Did you have any contact
during the day?

191
00:09:01,913 --> 00:09:03,749
He called at 9:30.

192
00:09:04,374 --> 00:09:07,210
Stressed, as usual.
Said he was gonna go to the driving range

193
00:09:07,335 --> 00:09:09,588
- before he came home.
- Was that a normal routine?

194
00:09:10,047 --> 00:09:12,632
Micah didn't like to bring
his work problems home with him

195
00:09:12,799 --> 00:09:15,385
so he would sort it out
on the driving range.

196
00:09:15,510 --> 00:09:17,137
So you think he was
facing a work problem?

197
00:09:17,471 --> 00:09:18,972
Yeah, it was some kind
of personnel problem.

198
00:09:19,097 --> 00:09:20,807
- Did he say what it was?
- No, no.

199
00:09:20,974 --> 00:09:22,976
Micah's job came
with a bull's eye attached.

200
00:09:23,226 --> 00:09:25,145
Somebody was always mad at him
for something.

201
00:09:27,272 --> 00:09:32,152
Last week, this letter came from
the husband of a transplant candidate.

202
00:09:33,361 --> 00:09:34,404
I thought you should see it.

203
00:09:35,530 --> 00:09:37,199
Micah was head
of the transplant board.

204
00:09:38,283 --> 00:09:40,535
He had to make hard decisions...

205
00:09:41,453 --> 00:09:43,121
Who lived and who died.

206
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:48,293
I told him he should go
and take that to the police

207
00:09:48,418 --> 00:09:50,045
but he said it was nothing
to worry about.

208
00:09:50,212 --> 00:09:52,881
"If my wife dies, you're the
son of a bitch I'm coming for first."

209
00:09:54,508 --> 00:09:55,550
Thank you.

210
00:09:56,218 --> 00:09:59,179
We have a new patient at the top
of the kidney transplant list...

211
00:09:59,971 --> 00:10:01,515
Patient Siberia.

212
00:10:02,724 --> 00:10:04,518
His, kidney function's
at a critical stage.

213
00:10:04,643 --> 00:10:06,103
Dr. Watson will give us a rundown.

214
00:10:06,228 --> 00:10:09,189
Wh-What about Enid Jordan?
She won't last another week.

215
00:10:09,314 --> 00:10:10,816
That's who Newton
had at the top of the list.

216
00:10:10,982 --> 00:10:12,192
Due to tragic circumstances

217
00:10:12,359 --> 00:10:15,487
Dr. Newton's no longer running
this meeting. I am.

218
00:10:16,530 --> 00:10:18,156
And as a member
of the anesthesia service

219
00:10:18,281 --> 00:10:22,119
Dr. Gidry, you are merely here
in an advisory role.

220
00:10:22,953 --> 00:10:23,995
Watson?

221
00:10:24,121 --> 00:10:26,039
Patient Siberia
has end-stage renal failure.

222
00:10:26,748 --> 00:10:27,791
Yes?

223
00:10:27,916 --> 00:10:29,209
Why do they call it
a kangaroo court?

224
00:10:29,459 --> 00:10:33,213
Are kangaroos especially unjust
in comparison to other marsupials?

225
00:10:33,338 --> 00:10:34,965
Would wallabies be more judicious?

226
00:10:35,549 --> 00:10:36,800
You promised
you wouldn't say anything.

227
00:10:36,967 --> 00:10:38,635
- He promised he wouldn't say anything.
- It's just a little...

228
00:10:38,760 --> 00:10:42,389
- This is not a kangaroo court.
- Did I say it was?

229
00:10:43,473 --> 00:10:46,268
Interesting that you deny
an unmade accusation.

230
00:10:47,144 --> 00:10:49,521
- Now that you raise the issue...
- I'm sorry.

231
00:10:50,772 --> 00:10:51,815
Who is this man?

232
00:10:52,357 --> 00:10:55,527
Oh, he's Patrick Jane.
He's a consultant with the CBI.

233
00:10:55,694 --> 00:10:56,987
- Hi.
- I'm agent Teresa Lisbon.

234
00:10:57,154 --> 00:10:59,239
We're investigating
the murder of Dr. Newton.

235
00:10:59,948 --> 00:11:03,785
- Well, this is hardly the venue.
- On the contrary. This is just the venue.

236
00:11:03,910 --> 00:11:05,078
A roomful of professionals

237
00:11:05,203 --> 00:11:06,705
who prescribe drugs
they know little about

238
00:11:06,830 --> 00:11:09,666
to cure diseases they know less about
for people they know nothing about

239
00:11:09,791 --> 00:11:11,251
and they call me a fraud.

240
00:11:11,710 --> 00:11:16,548
Now by the raise of the hand,
which one of you killed Dr. Newton?

241
00:11:17,716 --> 00:11:19,259
You're gonna stand by
and watch this?

242
00:11:19,467 --> 00:11:21,011
Ah, it's out of my control.

243
00:11:21,178 --> 00:11:24,431
My boss is agent Kimball Cho.
I can give you his phone number.

244
00:11:25,724 --> 00:11:26,766
Well, I won't put up with it.

245
00:11:26,892 --> 00:11:28,810
Oh, come, now.
It's perfectly obvious.

246
00:11:29,060 --> 00:11:31,229
Patient Siberia gets first dibs
on a kidney

247
00:11:31,354 --> 00:11:33,857
because he's some V.I.P.
with oodles of cash.

248
00:11:34,065 --> 00:11:35,150
Now that you're in charge

249
00:11:35,317 --> 00:11:37,652
it's all velvet rope
for the V.I.P.S, right?

250
00:11:39,821 --> 00:11:40,864
Meeting adjourned.

251
00:11:41,489 --> 00:11:43,825
Oh, and, uh, for those of you
who are less experienced

252
00:11:43,992 --> 00:11:45,035
with police intimidation

253
00:11:45,160 --> 00:11:46,912
you're under no obligation
to talk to these two.

254
00:11:48,038 --> 00:11:49,289
- Smooth.
- Thank you.

255
00:11:49,414 --> 00:11:50,707
- Give 'em hell.
- I will.

256
00:11:50,916 --> 00:11:53,543
- You're Dr. Quick's accomplice, yes?
- Surgery fellow.

257
00:11:54,336 --> 00:11:56,004
- Scared of doctors, eh?
- No.

258
00:11:56,171 --> 00:11:58,089
I understand.
Don't like some of them myself.

259
00:11:58,840 --> 00:12:01,343
Since Dr. Quick isn't interested
in talking to us

260
00:12:01,468 --> 00:12:03,637
perhaps you can tell us
where he was last night.

261
00:12:03,845 --> 00:12:06,348
You think he had something to do
with Dr. Newton's murder?

262
00:12:06,890 --> 00:12:09,809
- Why?
- Elementary, my dear Vernon.

263
00:12:10,143 --> 00:12:11,478
Newton's body isn't even cold

264
00:12:11,645 --> 00:12:13,271
and quick has seized
his position with Gusto.

265
00:12:13,396 --> 00:12:16,149
- The man lives up to his name.
- Dr. Quick didn't kill anyone.

266
00:12:16,691 --> 00:12:18,693
He just wants us to be
a top-notch research hospital.

267
00:12:18,818 --> 00:12:21,196
For that, we need money.
We're not a charity.

268
00:12:21,529 --> 00:12:22,948
You still haven't answered
my question.

269
00:12:23,156 --> 00:12:25,867
- Where was Dr. Quick last night?
- He had a dinner.

270
00:12:26,076 --> 00:12:28,286
It was running late, so he
asked me to cover his call.

271
00:12:28,495 --> 00:12:30,914
- I worked throughout the night.
- Late dinner.

272
00:12:31,206 --> 00:12:32,958
You obviously haven't partied
with pharmaceutical reps.

273
00:12:33,083 --> 00:12:35,168
- "Operator."
- We need Dr. Montez in I.C.U.

274
00:12:35,961 --> 00:12:39,381
- And who's this patient Siberia?
- A kidney transplant candidate

275
00:12:39,506 --> 00:12:41,508
who is patiently waiting
for me in the C.C.U.

276
00:12:42,050 --> 00:12:44,344
- If you'll excuse me, please.
- "Dr. Montez to I.C.U."

277
00:12:44,636 --> 00:12:46,221
"Dr. Montez to I.C.U."

278
00:12:46,763 --> 00:12:49,683
Let's head over to radiology.
That badge is still buggin' me.

279
00:12:49,891 --> 00:12:51,559
I wanna know why
it was so radioactive.

280
00:12:51,810 --> 00:12:53,478
I'm gonna pass.
I'm off the cafeteria

281
00:12:53,603 --> 00:12:56,189
for something deliciously
suspended in gelatin.

282
00:12:56,773 --> 00:12:58,566
I'm not even gonna ask you
where you're really going.

283
00:12:58,692 --> 00:12:59,734
You wanna know why?

284
00:13:00,819 --> 00:13:01,861
I don't have to.

285
00:13:09,577 --> 00:13:11,454
- Hi, Byron.
- Hey.

286
00:13:11,746 --> 00:13:12,789
I'm agent Van Pelt.

287
00:13:13,957 --> 00:13:16,209
- Your wife is Enid Jordan?
- Yeah, that's right.

288
00:13:16,751 --> 00:13:18,878
Last week the head
of the transplant board

289
00:13:19,004 --> 00:13:21,006
at blessed sacrament
received this.

290
00:13:21,673 --> 00:13:22,716
Did you write it?

291
00:13:23,758 --> 00:13:27,721
You know, they say if you're
angry to write a letter

292
00:13:28,096 --> 00:13:29,639
but wait a day
before you send it.

293
00:13:29,848 --> 00:13:32,434
They say sometimes just the act
of writing is enough.

294
00:13:33,852 --> 00:13:34,978
I waited a week.

295
00:13:36,396 --> 00:13:38,648
And I still felt every word.

296
00:13:39,941 --> 00:13:41,651
So, yes, I sent it.

297
00:13:43,028 --> 00:13:45,280
You do know that Dr. Newton
was murdered last night?

298
00:13:46,364 --> 00:13:48,199
Yes, and I'm sorry about that.

299
00:13:48,616 --> 00:13:51,578
But tragedy happens.
Ask Enid.

300
00:13:51,953 --> 00:13:53,788
Why were you so angry
with Dr. Newton?

301
00:13:54,039 --> 00:13:55,915
He put your wife
on the transplant list.

302
00:13:56,374 --> 00:13:58,752
Do you know what it took
to get into his program?

303
00:13:59,753 --> 00:14:04,424
First, Enid had to lose the required
weight through sickness.

304
00:14:05,258 --> 00:14:06,926
And then she was too sick.

305
00:14:07,969 --> 00:14:11,848
And then after that, can we
afford to maintain a new kidney?

306
00:14:12,098 --> 00:14:14,351
Hoop after hoop after hoop.

307
00:14:14,601 --> 00:14:18,229
- But she was put on the list.
- And nothing changed.

308
00:14:18,605 --> 00:14:21,066
You're up the list one day,
down the next

309
00:14:21,649 --> 00:14:25,070
never at the top, and always
there's someone else

310
00:14:25,195 --> 00:14:28,698
that gets to go first.
I'm so tired, lady.

311
00:14:29,699 --> 00:14:31,993
Byron, where were you
at 2:00 this morning?

312
00:14:33,745 --> 00:14:36,456
I was, uh, bent over a toilet

313
00:14:37,332 --> 00:14:39,793
holding my wife's hair back
while she spit up blood.

314
00:14:40,710 --> 00:14:42,003
Stress ulcers.

315
00:14:42,962 --> 00:14:45,298
And so back into the hospital
she went this morning.

316
00:14:48,385 --> 00:14:50,845
Another de-clotting procedure
this afternoon.

317
00:14:54,933 --> 00:14:56,559
How many times
can they cut her open?

318
00:15:14,452 --> 00:15:15,495
"Operator."

319
00:15:15,620 --> 00:15:19,249
Hi. We need Dr. Watson
in the O.R., stat.

320
00:15:19,374 --> 00:15:22,001
- "Which room, sir?"
- Three.

321
00:15:22,210 --> 00:15:23,253
"Paging him now."

322
00:15:26,214 --> 00:15:28,341
"Dr. Watson to O.R. 3, stat."

323
00:15:28,967 --> 00:15:30,927
"Dr. Watson to O.R. 3, stat."

324
00:15:50,572 --> 00:15:52,323
You must be patient Siberia.

325
00:15:53,241 --> 00:15:54,784
Yeah, well I... Oh!

326
00:15:57,579 --> 00:15:58,663
No movement.

327
00:15:59,664 --> 00:16:00,707
No.

328
00:16:09,589 --> 00:16:12,633
Who are you?
And don't say "doctor."

329
00:16:13,301 --> 00:16:15,928
Wasn't going to.
I'm Patrick Jane.

330
00:16:16,053 --> 00:16:20,016
And I'm kind of...
Law enforcement.

331
00:16:20,808 --> 00:16:24,520
You must be some kind
of Russian crime lord, yes?

332
00:16:26,105 --> 00:16:30,151
- Where's your badge?
- Front vest pocket.

333
00:16:32,695 --> 00:16:35,198
It's more of a laminate.
I-I didn't get the, uh...

334
00:16:36,157 --> 00:16:39,243
I'm a consultant.
I didn't get the real shiny badge.

335
00:16:40,119 --> 00:16:42,955
Who tells you
I'm Russian crime lord?

336
00:16:43,372 --> 00:16:49,086
Your Sochi accent, the star tattoo
on your chest the bullet wounds

337
00:16:49,378 --> 00:16:51,547
your thousand-yard stare.
I could go on.

338
00:17:01,766 --> 00:17:02,808
Thank you.

339
00:17:06,729 --> 00:17:07,772
Rubens.

340
00:17:08,523 --> 00:17:11,901
- My name is Ulis Oratni.
- Yeah.

341
00:17:15,154 --> 00:17:16,489
Why are you here?

342
00:17:17,448 --> 00:17:19,784
Well, a doctor at the hospital
was murdered.

343
00:17:19,992 --> 00:17:22,161
His name is Micah Newton.

344
00:17:22,662 --> 00:17:25,665
And he stood between you
and a...

345
00:17:26,791 --> 00:17:27,833
New kidney.

346
00:17:30,169 --> 00:17:31,337
You think I killed him.

347
00:17:31,462 --> 00:17:35,216
No. Obviously, you're not in good enough
shape for such strenuous activity

348
00:17:35,341 --> 00:17:39,345
but possibly someone you know did...
Someone, uh, strong like bull.

349
00:17:40,263 --> 00:17:41,305
How's your golf swing?

350
00:17:42,139 --> 00:17:43,516
Give me club.
I will show you.

351
00:17:45,601 --> 00:17:46,936
Got the pa...
what's going on here?

352
00:17:47,061 --> 00:17:49,939
This... this man... he has a gun
and he pointed it at me.

353
00:17:50,106 --> 00:17:52,650
He's very rude and that's not even
including the assault.

354
00:17:52,900 --> 00:17:55,194
Sir, I'm with the CBI.
Is he telling the truth?

355
00:17:56,654 --> 00:17:58,781
Get up against the wall. Go.

356
00:18:00,366 --> 00:18:02,326
It's your colleague that's trespassing.

357
00:18:02,910 --> 00:18:04,537
And he's put the safety
of this patient at risk.

358
00:18:04,662 --> 00:18:06,247
His blood pressure's skyrocketed.

359
00:18:06,664 --> 00:18:08,541
We're leaving,
but we're taking him with us.

360
00:18:08,916 --> 00:18:09,959
Come on.

361
00:18:12,211 --> 00:18:13,754
Oh, just one more thing...

362
00:18:13,879 --> 00:18:15,673
What's the going price
for a kidney these days?

363
00:18:15,840 --> 00:18:18,593
Is it an x-ray machine
or a new wing on the hospital?

364
00:18:18,718 --> 00:18:21,554
Or does Ivan the terrible here
have Dr. Quick's niece

365
00:18:21,679 --> 00:18:22,888
tied up somewhere
in some basement?

366
00:18:23,014 --> 00:18:25,516
- Go. Now!
- Bye.

367
00:18:29,353 --> 00:18:31,272
I just got off the phone with Interpol.

368
00:18:31,439 --> 00:18:35,985
Yegor Golenka our Russian friend in holding,
has an extensive police record In Moscow.

369
00:18:36,152 --> 00:18:37,278
I'm gonna have
a word with him about it.

370
00:18:37,486 --> 00:18:39,697
What did you find out about Dr. Newton's
radiation badge at the hospital?

371
00:18:39,864 --> 00:18:40,906
I talked to his assistant

372
00:18:41,032 --> 00:18:42,950
then I asked around
in the radiology department.

373
00:18:43,075 --> 00:18:46,370
Nobody could explain why his radiation
levels were so high. It's a mystery.

374
00:18:46,829 --> 00:18:48,956
Did you find out what source
of radioactivity would affect the badge

375
00:18:49,081 --> 00:18:50,249
and not the person wearing the badge?

376
00:18:52,376 --> 00:18:53,419
No.

377
00:18:53,544 --> 00:18:55,046
Okay. Van Pelt, follow up
on that for me, would you?

378
00:18:55,171 --> 00:18:57,089
- Will do.
- I can handle it.

379
00:18:58,215 --> 00:18:59,467
Don't you have to go
talk to your suspect?

380
00:19:02,011 --> 00:19:03,054
Yes, boss.

381
00:19:12,396 --> 00:19:14,732
We hear you're a violent offender
in Russia.

382
00:19:17,151 --> 00:19:18,653
How'd you come by
your weapon here?

383
00:19:24,075 --> 00:19:26,077
I can get you a translator
if you need one.

384
00:19:27,328 --> 00:19:28,371
I understand.

385
00:19:29,038 --> 00:19:32,792
Well, in that case, speak up and look me
in the eye when you talk to me.

386
00:19:33,376 --> 00:19:34,460
Show some respect.

387
00:19:36,962 --> 00:19:38,005
Yes, ma'am.

388
00:19:38,714 --> 00:19:39,840
Let's try again.

389
00:19:40,675 --> 00:19:43,511
- How did you get the gun?
- I found it.

390
00:19:44,095 --> 00:19:46,889
These guns... they practically
grow on trees in California.

391
00:19:47,223 --> 00:19:48,641
You know that in this country

392
00:19:48,808 --> 00:19:50,726
you need to have a license
to have a gun.

393
00:19:52,186 --> 00:19:54,230
And when you threw my colleague
up against the wall

394
00:19:54,355 --> 00:19:56,399
and held him at gunpoint,
you committed a felony.

395
00:19:57,108 --> 00:19:58,651
That means you go to jail.

396
00:20:00,569 --> 00:20:04,740
Your prison system is, uh...
Like vacation in Russia.

397
00:20:05,241 --> 00:20:07,201
But then who would
look after Mr. Oratni?

398
00:20:08,828 --> 00:20:10,121
My replacement.

399
00:20:11,038 --> 00:20:14,417
- You'd do anything for him, wouldn't you?
- Without hesitation.

400
00:20:14,792 --> 00:20:16,919
- Would you kill for him?
- Of course.

401
00:20:17,378 --> 00:20:18,796
Did you kill Dr. Newton for him?

402
00:20:21,716 --> 00:20:22,758
No.

403
00:20:22,925 --> 00:20:24,844
Where were you last night
between 9:00 and 2:00?

404
00:20:25,469 --> 00:20:29,140
Watching over Mr. Oratni...
In his room.

405
00:20:31,100 --> 00:20:32,143
All night.

406
00:20:32,476 --> 00:20:36,147
Dr. Quick... he, uh, made special
provision for me to be there.

407
00:20:37,773 --> 00:20:39,066
Since arriving in this country

408
00:20:39,191 --> 00:20:42,236
I have not left the side of Mr. Oratni
for a single moment.

409
00:20:43,696 --> 00:20:44,739
Until now.

410
00:20:48,242 --> 00:20:49,785
That's the nurse's station there.

411
00:20:50,035 --> 00:20:52,329
If you need anything else,
please don't ask me.

412
00:20:52,455 --> 00:20:54,039
You got me in so much trouble
this morning.

413
00:20:54,206 --> 00:20:55,916
I'm sorry, Francine.
Thank you.

414
00:20:56,667 --> 00:20:59,795
"Paging Dr. Bender,
Paging Dr. Bender."

415
00:21:00,588 --> 00:21:04,383
- Looking for a post-op patient?
- No. I'm, uh, looking for a nurse.

416
00:21:04,592 --> 00:21:05,885
- Which one?
- You, actually.

417
00:21:06,051 --> 00:21:09,388
You're in the seat of power here and
we all know who really runs a hospital.

418
00:21:09,513 --> 00:21:13,934
Please? Can somebody please help me?
Will you help my wife?

419
00:21:14,059 --> 00:21:16,812
She just got out of surgery.
She says her pain is unbearable.

420
00:21:17,438 --> 00:21:19,106
Hang in there, baby.

421
00:21:19,231 --> 00:21:20,941
Enid Jordan.
Did she get her kidney?

422
00:21:21,066 --> 00:21:24,153
No, just another de-clotting procedure,
more tubes stuck in her body.

423
00:21:24,278 --> 00:21:25,988
I don't know how much more she can take.

424
00:21:26,197 --> 00:21:27,239
Dr. Gidry.

425
00:21:28,073 --> 00:21:29,700
- Still rabble-rousing?
- Always.

426
00:21:30,242 --> 00:21:33,120
She's post-op 15 minutes
after a de-clotting procedure

427
00:21:33,245 --> 00:21:34,413
and severely agitated.

428
00:21:34,538 --> 00:21:38,334
Okay. Mrs. Jordan, it's Dr. Gidry
Your anesthesiologist.

429
00:21:38,501 --> 00:21:41,378
- Where are you on the pain scale?
- Oh, come on! She's in agony!

430
00:21:41,629 --> 00:21:42,713
What does it look like?

431
00:21:44,340 --> 00:21:47,927
I'm afraid your wife has reached her
allowable amount of post-op pain medication.

432
00:21:48,469 --> 00:21:50,513
I need you to hang on
a little longer, okay, honey?

433
00:21:51,555 --> 00:21:54,266
Push 10 milligrams of Valium
if she's still agitated in 20 minutes.

434
00:21:54,391 --> 00:21:57,686
What is wrong with you people?
I'm sorry, baby.

435
00:21:57,895 --> 00:22:00,105
I, I'll keep trying.
I'm not gonna give up.

436
00:22:00,314 --> 00:22:01,941
Excuse me, ma'am, if... if I may?

437
00:22:03,484 --> 00:22:06,195
You might wanna try screaming.
Often helps.

438
00:22:06,320 --> 00:22:07,363
Excuse me?

439
00:22:07,488 --> 00:22:10,699
Screaming. Expressing the pain.
Saint whoever-it-is would agree.

440
00:22:10,866 --> 00:22:12,368
Screaming... it's therapeutic in itself.

441
00:22:12,910 --> 00:22:15,246
Besides, it'll get you your drugs
a lot quicker.

442
00:22:15,538 --> 00:22:18,040
- Who are you?
- Patrick Jane. Nice to meet you.

443
00:22:18,707 --> 00:22:22,086
- Byron and Enid, yes?
- Yeah.

444
00:22:22,336 --> 00:22:23,671
Scream. Try it.

445
00:22:34,181 --> 00:22:35,975
- Russian doesn't look good for it?
- Nope.

446
00:22:38,143 --> 00:22:39,186
- Hey, boss.
- Hey.

447
00:22:39,311 --> 00:22:40,354
Hi.

448
00:22:40,479 --> 00:22:42,773
I was looking into the radiation badge
and learned something.

449
00:22:43,107 --> 00:22:45,109
Any access in the hospital after hours

450
00:22:45,234 --> 00:22:47,903
requires employees to use their I.D.
badge to gain entry.

451
00:22:48,237 --> 00:22:50,197
- That sounds promising.
- There's more.

452
00:22:50,614 --> 00:22:53,117
Newton's badge usage the night
of the murder doesn't add up.

453
00:22:53,450 --> 00:22:54,493
How so?

454
00:22:54,618 --> 00:22:57,872
According to the security report,
he swiped his badge in radiology

455
00:22:58,038 --> 00:22:59,164
at 8:05 that night.

456
00:22:59,331 --> 00:23:01,375
But Newton's assistant said that
he was giving a lecture

457
00:23:01,542 --> 00:23:02,960
to medical students
around that time.

458
00:23:03,127 --> 00:23:05,462
Exactly. Kind of hard to be
in two places at once, right?

459
00:23:05,588 --> 00:23:07,006
We'll run that down tomorrow
and see where it leads.

460
00:23:07,131 --> 00:23:08,757
- Good work, Van Pelt.
- Good work.

461
00:23:08,924 --> 00:23:09,967
Thanks.

462
00:23:10,092 --> 00:23:12,219
Well, you were right.
The radiation badge was a clue.

463
00:23:12,595 --> 00:23:15,139
Just doing what you taught me.
Running down all the angles.

464
00:23:15,723 --> 00:23:16,765
Yeah.

465
00:23:17,016 --> 00:23:18,058
Listen, boss...

466
00:23:18,183 --> 00:23:21,645
Don't call me "boss."
I'm not your boss. You're my boss.

467
00:23:27,109 --> 00:23:28,152
Give it a try.

468
00:23:29,904 --> 00:23:32,156
Come on, little more than that,
little more than that. Everyone.

469
00:23:35,576 --> 00:23:36,869
The girl's got pipes.

470
00:23:41,457 --> 00:23:42,541
How does that feel?

471
00:23:43,125 --> 00:23:44,543
- Feels good.
- Pretty good.

472
00:23:44,877 --> 00:23:46,503
Scream a day
keeps the doctor away.

473
00:23:47,880 --> 00:23:50,215
I would steer clear of the tall one,
if I were you.

474
00:23:50,341 --> 00:23:51,717
Nothing but heartache there.

475
00:23:53,719 --> 00:23:55,054
How did you know...

476
00:23:55,346 --> 00:24:00,059
Oh, my God. I have been telling Gloria
he was a dog for weeks.

477
00:24:00,267 --> 00:24:02,102
Yes, but he is a yummy dawg.

478
00:24:02,853 --> 00:24:04,855
So level with me.
Most of the doctors around here...

479
00:24:05,147 --> 00:24:07,775
- Terrible, right?
- No, some of 'em are keepers.

480
00:24:08,651 --> 00:24:11,487
Dr. Newton was an absolute treasure,
bless his heart.

481
00:24:11,946 --> 00:24:12,988
Who else?

482
00:24:13,113 --> 00:24:15,991
On the principle that he with the whitest
coat hides the darkest heart

483
00:24:16,116 --> 00:24:18,369
who do you think is the nicest,
sweetest doctor here?

484
00:24:18,869 --> 00:24:20,496
- Dr. Watson.
- Dr. Watson.

485
00:24:21,956 --> 00:24:22,998
That's interesting.

486
00:24:23,707 --> 00:24:25,000
You think he's the killer?

487
00:24:25,626 --> 00:24:27,503
Well, he is Dr. Quick's yes-man

488
00:24:27,628 --> 00:24:30,089
and the supervising physician
for patient Siberia

489
00:24:30,255 --> 00:24:31,590
so that puts him
right in the thick of things.

490
00:24:31,715 --> 00:24:37,012
No. Dr. Watson is cute...
And nice.

491
00:24:37,221 --> 00:24:38,764
I, I was working a double last night

492
00:24:38,889 --> 00:24:41,517
and he got doughnuts for everyone
on the graveyard shift.

493
00:24:42,351 --> 00:24:45,521
You mean, whilst he was covering
for Dr. Quick's shift

494
00:24:45,646 --> 00:24:47,314
he went out and bought
everyone doughnuts?

495
00:24:47,564 --> 00:24:49,608
You should be marrying him, Daisy.

496
00:24:50,275 --> 00:24:51,902
Dr. Watson wasn't working here
last night.

497
00:24:52,027 --> 00:24:54,279
He just... Stopped by.

498
00:24:54,905 --> 00:24:56,740
Doctors really are the best liars,
aren't they?

499
00:24:57,282 --> 00:25:00,035
So is Dr. Watson
working right now?

500
00:25:00,285 --> 00:25:02,121
Yeah, but his shift
ends in a half-hour.

501
00:25:02,246 --> 00:25:04,623
- You want me to page him for you?
- Oh, no, no, no. I'll find him.

502
00:25:04,999 --> 00:25:06,041
It's been a lot of fun.

503
00:25:06,625 --> 00:25:08,419
Everything we've said
is in strict confidence.

504
00:25:08,627 --> 00:25:11,255
I'll make that official
by deputizing each one of you.

505
00:25:11,797 --> 00:25:13,173
It's our little secret, ladies.

506
00:25:26,854 --> 00:25:28,522
What is he doing
in this neighborhood?

507
00:25:29,106 --> 00:25:30,733
That's what you're here
to find out.

508
00:25:31,358 --> 00:25:34,028
Dr. Watson lied about
working at the hospital.

509
00:25:34,236 --> 00:25:38,115
He merely did a drive-by
with doughnuts

510
00:25:39,283 --> 00:25:40,701
in the middle
of the murder window.

511
00:25:42,453 --> 00:25:44,204
Probably looking for an alibi.

512
00:25:44,621 --> 00:25:46,707
Hospital's only a few minutes away
from the driving range.

513
00:25:47,833 --> 00:25:50,794
Entering a sketchy building
with a duffel bag...

514
00:25:51,628 --> 00:25:53,922
Possibly full of money
to pay off the killer.

515
00:25:54,757 --> 00:25:58,093
That's your cue to be a hero.
I'll wait in the car.

516
00:25:59,928 --> 00:26:01,638
- Thanks.
- Go get 'em.

517
00:26:20,074 --> 00:26:22,659
- "Get away from me!"
- "Alcia, stop! Alcia!"

518
00:26:22,785 --> 00:26:25,913
- Leave me alone! Leave me alone!
- CBI!

519
00:26:26,038 --> 00:26:27,581
- Hands in the air!
- Help!

520
00:26:36,213 --> 00:26:38,715
- It hurts!
- What's wrong with her?

521
00:26:38,840 --> 00:26:40,759
She's a heroin addict
coming out of an overdose.

522
00:26:40,884 --> 00:26:43,386
I need to continue helping her...
Now!

523
00:26:43,595 --> 00:26:44,638
Should I call for an ambulance?

524
00:26:45,680 --> 00:26:48,767
No need. Alicia? Alicia, it's okay.
It's okay. You're fine.

525
00:26:51,228 --> 00:26:52,687
Another dose should do the trick.

526
00:26:54,815 --> 00:26:55,857
- No!
- What is that?

527
00:26:57,984 --> 00:27:00,737
Naloxone. Fastest way to strip opiates
from the system

528
00:27:01,363 --> 00:27:02,405
reverse an overdose.

529
00:27:05,367 --> 00:27:06,827
Always keep it handy
in my bag.

530
00:27:08,203 --> 00:27:10,080
Good thing one of her smack
buddies called me in time.

531
00:27:11,832 --> 00:27:14,459
This is more than altruistic.
Do you have an addict in the family?

532
00:27:14,918 --> 00:27:16,545
My mother OD'd
when I was 12.

533
00:27:17,003 --> 00:27:18,421
It's part of the reason
I became a doctor.

534
00:27:18,672 --> 00:27:20,006
Why did you lie about
being in the hospital

535
00:27:20,132 --> 00:27:21,383
the night that Newton
was murdered?

536
00:27:24,761 --> 00:27:27,013
I was moonlighting
at a mobile clinic last night.

537
00:27:27,681 --> 00:27:29,891
That's a violation of my contract
with the hospital.

538
00:27:31,143 --> 00:27:32,310
I can't afford to lose my job.

539
00:27:32,435 --> 00:27:34,688
I've got medical school bills
like you wouldn't believe.

540
00:27:36,148 --> 00:27:39,109
Okay. Well, keep up
the good work. Rigsby?

541
00:27:39,359 --> 00:27:41,111
I'm sorry. This man's still a suspect.

542
00:27:41,611 --> 00:27:43,697
If Newton found out about his moonlighting
that could be motive for murder.

543
00:27:43,822 --> 00:27:44,865
Newton knew.

544
00:27:45,115 --> 00:27:47,284
He even came to the clinic
to keep his skills up

545
00:27:47,617 --> 00:27:48,660
give back to the community.

546
00:27:48,869 --> 00:27:50,787
Regular saint.
See? There you go.

547
00:27:51,121 --> 00:27:53,331
It's obvious Watson here
is a diamond in the rough.

548
00:27:53,748 --> 00:27:57,544
One doctor clear, a whole hospital
full of suspects to go.

549
00:28:05,302 --> 00:28:09,472
"Dr. Staitman to I.C.U.,
Dr. Staitman to I.C.U."

550
00:28:20,609 --> 00:28:21,651
Seven minutes.

551
00:28:22,444 --> 00:28:23,862
I should have hurdled
that last gurney.

552
00:28:24,029 --> 00:28:25,071
Right.

553
00:28:25,197 --> 00:28:27,490
What? I ran track in high school.

554
00:28:27,657 --> 00:28:30,702
The medical students I talked to said
that Newton's lecture started at 8:10

555
00:28:30,911 --> 00:28:33,788
but his badge was swiped
in radiology at 8:05.

556
00:28:34,247 --> 00:28:36,917
That means he had five minutes to make
the same trip that took you seven.

557
00:28:37,083 --> 00:28:38,376
And I was running fast.

558
00:28:38,752 --> 00:28:42,214
So Newton was either faster than you
or someone else was using his badge.

559
00:28:42,422 --> 00:28:44,549
Somebody stole his badge, definitely.

560
00:28:46,801 --> 00:28:48,720
What? I'm fast.

561
00:28:51,014 --> 00:28:52,057
Because of his position

562
00:28:52,182 --> 00:28:54,559
Newton's badge allowed him access
to every area of the hospital.

563
00:28:54,684 --> 00:28:55,727
Valuable badge to have.

564
00:28:55,852 --> 00:28:56,895
And over the last month

565
00:28:57,020 --> 00:28:58,605
Newton accessed
the radiology department

566
00:28:58,730 --> 00:29:00,482
three times as much as any other area.

567
00:29:00,607 --> 00:29:01,900
But the people you interviewed in radiology

568
00:29:02,025 --> 00:29:04,110
- said that Newton rarely spent time there.
- Exactly.

569
00:29:04,277 --> 00:29:06,780
Somebody else was using Newton's
badge the night of the murder.

570
00:29:06,947 --> 00:29:07,989
Show him.

571
00:29:08,240 --> 00:29:09,783
Newton's lectures are videotaped.

572
00:29:09,908 --> 00:29:12,077
This is a still image
hours before Newton was killed.

573
00:29:13,453 --> 00:29:15,830
He's not wearing his security badge.
Was it reported stolen?

574
00:29:16,081 --> 00:29:18,333
No, but we believe the badge was used
at the time

575
00:29:18,458 --> 00:29:20,043
by someone he thought
he could trust with it...

576
00:29:20,543 --> 00:29:22,170
Francine Trent, his assistant.

577
00:29:22,837 --> 00:29:25,382
I ran her financials.
She used her credit card two hours ago.

578
00:29:25,715 --> 00:29:27,717
- Bought a ticket at the main bus terminal.
- Let's hit it.

579
00:29:37,143 --> 00:29:38,478
The women's restroom is clear.

580
00:29:42,357 --> 00:29:43,525
Concession area clear.

581
00:29:52,534 --> 00:29:54,494
Suspect spotted,
northwest corner.

582
00:29:56,579 --> 00:29:57,622
Are you going somewhere?

583
00:30:00,166 --> 00:30:01,209
What is this?

584
00:30:01,334 --> 00:30:03,211
We know you stole
Dr. Newton's security pass

585
00:30:03,336 --> 00:30:04,379
the night of the murder.

586
00:30:04,504 --> 00:30:06,923
When did you return it?
Before or after you killed him?

587
00:30:07,382 --> 00:30:08,466
I didn't kill Dr. Newton.

588
00:30:08,633 --> 00:30:10,343
- You're gonna have to come with us.
- First we need to look in that case.

589
00:30:10,468 --> 00:30:12,053
- Don't touch that!
- Okay.

590
00:30:12,762 --> 00:30:15,807
- What's in the suitcase?
- Cesium-137.

591
00:30:16,308 --> 00:30:18,518
The suitcase is lead-lined,
but if you open it unprotected

592
00:30:18,643 --> 00:30:21,354
the material will get into your
marrow and mutate your cells.

593
00:30:21,896 --> 00:30:24,024
That's what she was using
Newton's all-access badge for.

594
00:30:24,316 --> 00:30:26,568
Those pellets sell for a small
fortune on the black market.

595
00:30:26,776 --> 00:30:28,695
And that explains
all the radiology visits

596
00:30:28,820 --> 00:30:31,573
and why, when I first met you,
you knew so much about it.

597
00:30:31,906 --> 00:30:34,117
Did Newton find out you stole them?
Is that why you killed him?

598
00:30:34,242 --> 00:30:36,911
I didn't kill anyone.
I, I spent the night at my boyfriend's.

599
00:30:37,037 --> 00:30:38,079
You can check.

600
00:30:38,204 --> 00:30:39,414
Rigsby, I want a Hazmat team
down here asap.

601
00:30:39,581 --> 00:30:41,875
Van Pelt, keep the perimeter secure
and keep an eye on the suspect.

602
00:30:42,000 --> 00:30:44,878
Lisbon. I don't think she's our killer.

603
00:30:45,211 --> 00:30:46,254
How can you be so sure?

604
00:30:46,379 --> 00:30:47,672
I believe her story,
and she's not a doctor.

605
00:30:48,089 --> 00:30:49,132
You, too?

606
00:30:52,802 --> 00:30:54,304
That's Dr. Malvo.

607
00:30:54,637 --> 00:30:57,349
Needs to remind himself
which limb he's cutting into.

608
00:30:57,640 --> 00:31:00,268
- Otherwise harmless.
- Unless you're his patient.

609
00:31:03,271 --> 00:31:04,356
What's going on, Daisy?

610
00:31:05,357 --> 00:31:07,400
He has enough drugs inside him
to knock out an elephant.

611
00:31:07,525 --> 00:31:09,944
- It doesn't make sense.
- Sensing a pattern here.

612
00:31:10,278 --> 00:31:13,114
If I had a nickel for every pain complaint,
I'd own the joint.

613
00:31:18,036 --> 00:31:19,079
Wakey, wakey.

614
00:31:20,872 --> 00:31:22,415
I heard they found you a kidney.

615
00:31:23,708 --> 00:31:24,918
You all set for surgery?

616
00:31:26,795 --> 00:31:29,798
Yep, I can see the fear in your eyes.

617
00:31:30,340 --> 00:31:32,634
You have to be fearless
in your line of work

618
00:31:33,176 --> 00:31:36,137
and now you fear the pain
you've inflicted on others

619
00:31:36,262 --> 00:31:38,723
has come back to you
in the form of sickness.

620
00:31:40,683 --> 00:31:44,187
And I do believe
you might be right.

621
00:31:59,494 --> 00:32:02,914
Nothing like a fresh cup of joe
before you start the business

622
00:32:03,081 --> 00:32:05,583
- of swapping out organs.
- Thank you, Patrick.

623
00:32:06,501 --> 00:32:10,839
- Pleasure. And for the unsung...
- Patrick, you're too much.

624
00:32:13,800 --> 00:32:14,843
I want a coffee.

625
00:32:15,135 --> 00:32:17,929
You know, I have a very special
cup of tea here that you should try.

626
00:32:19,889 --> 00:32:23,518
And our crack leader
who will presently save the life

627
00:32:23,643 --> 00:32:26,187
of a ruthless foreign killer.
You definitely need a coffee.

628
00:32:26,938 --> 00:32:29,232
You don't belong here. Henry.

629
00:32:30,316 --> 00:32:32,944
Not very hospitable, but I get your drift.
Whoa, I'm leaving.

630
00:32:42,328 --> 00:32:45,081
Your murder victim's assistant
gave up her buyer.

631
00:32:45,457 --> 00:32:48,460
She's been stealing small amounts
from the hospital over the last month.

632
00:32:48,585 --> 00:32:50,128
Adds up to a huge profit.

633
00:32:50,795 --> 00:32:53,798
- The feds just picked the buyer up.
- That's a relief.

634
00:32:54,340 --> 00:32:58,678
Unfortunately, she has an airtight
alibi for the night of the murder.

635
00:32:58,803 --> 00:33:00,180
After she returned his badge

636
00:33:00,805 --> 00:33:04,058
she did indeed spend the night
with a male companion.

637
00:33:04,476 --> 00:33:06,227
So Newton's killer
is still out there.

638
00:33:07,228 --> 00:33:11,733
True, but those pellets could have
been weaponized in a dirty bomb

639
00:33:12,400 --> 00:33:14,444
with the power to injure
thousands of people.

640
00:33:16,821 --> 00:33:17,864
Nice catch.

641
00:33:18,531 --> 00:33:21,493
Wasn't my catch. Cho gets the credit.

642
00:33:23,244 --> 00:33:25,121
He's a good leader.
You were right about him.

643
00:33:27,081 --> 00:33:29,417
I'll include your sentiments in his file

644
00:33:30,668 --> 00:33:33,046
as well as a commendation
in your own.

645
00:33:34,088 --> 00:33:35,131
Thank you.

646
00:33:37,175 --> 00:33:40,303
You are back in charge of your team,
effective immediately.

647
00:33:42,096 --> 00:33:45,099
Wait... What?

648
00:33:48,019 --> 00:33:49,771
- You're back in charge.
- I heard you.

649
00:33:54,150 --> 00:33:55,985
Why was I pulled off
in the first place?

650
00:33:57,529 --> 00:33:58,863
Maybe I was
messing with you?

651
00:34:04,953 --> 00:34:08,039
And it showed you I won't
tolerate any disrespect.

652
00:34:17,173 --> 00:34:18,216
That'll be all.

653
00:34:23,054 --> 00:34:25,807
Lisbon, well done.
Very good news.

654
00:34:25,932 --> 00:34:29,394
I have the perfect
congratulatory gift in mind

655
00:34:29,769 --> 00:34:31,020
but you're gonna have to
come by the hospital

656
00:34:31,145 --> 00:34:32,438
so I can present it to you.

657
00:34:32,647 --> 00:34:34,857
"Patrick Jane, O.R. 8, stat."

658
00:34:35,191 --> 00:34:38,528
"If you can hear my voice, Patrick
move your ass to O.R. 8."

659
00:34:39,821 --> 00:34:40,863
Better make that quick.

660
00:34:41,531 --> 00:34:42,657
That was my ass.

661
00:34:46,911 --> 00:34:47,954
What the hell is this?

662
00:34:50,039 --> 00:34:52,041
I felt it important
to let you and your team know

663
00:34:52,166 --> 00:34:55,461
before you cut this man open,
that you have all been drugged.

664
00:34:55,670 --> 00:34:56,796
What are you talking about?

665
00:35:08,055 --> 00:35:09,265
What do you mean, drugged?

666
00:35:09,932 --> 00:35:10,975
How? Who did it?

667
00:35:11,767 --> 00:35:15,605
I did, by a special coffee blend.

668
00:35:16,439 --> 00:35:18,441
I got the idea
from the able Dr. Watson.

669
00:35:18,566 --> 00:35:20,651
What was that stuff you gave
to the heroin addict?

670
00:35:20,943 --> 00:35:22,361
- Naloxone?
- Yeah, that's it.

671
00:35:22,570 --> 00:35:24,196
It was handy in your duffel bag

672
00:35:24,488 --> 00:35:27,908
just as you said.
I put a "carefully measured dose"

673
00:35:28,034 --> 00:35:30,119
in the coffee pot... all of it.

674
00:35:31,162 --> 00:35:32,413
Why would you do that?

675
00:35:32,622 --> 00:35:36,500
Perhaps I should back this story up.
Somebody in this room is an addict

676
00:35:36,626 --> 00:35:38,544
who's been stealing pain-relieving drugs

677
00:35:38,669 --> 00:35:41,380
from the patients before,
during, or after surgery.

678
00:35:41,631 --> 00:35:44,091
- What makes you think that?
- From my time spent with you, dear.

679
00:35:44,508 --> 00:35:47,261
As soon as I saw those patients
fresh out of surgery

680
00:35:47,386 --> 00:35:50,473
it was obvious to me they hadn't been
given enough of the good stuff.

681
00:35:51,223 --> 00:35:53,517
And I believe that's what
Dr. Newton figured out

682
00:35:53,643 --> 00:35:55,144
and that's what got him killed.

683
00:35:56,395 --> 00:36:00,191
You drugged all of us,
based on that wild conjecture?

684
00:36:00,941 --> 00:36:01,984
Yes.

685
00:36:02,526 --> 00:36:04,487
- You gave everyone here naloxone?
- Yes!

686
00:36:04,945 --> 00:36:06,864
Do you have any idea
how dangerous that can be?

687
00:36:06,989 --> 00:36:09,033
Well, I did read the label,
thank you very much

688
00:36:09,200 --> 00:36:13,954
and it's only harmful to those individuals
suffering with liver and kidney damage...

689
00:36:14,080 --> 00:36:17,291
Uh, that makes Oratni completely
out of the question...

690
00:36:17,583 --> 00:36:18,626
And pregnant women.

691
00:36:19,418 --> 00:36:22,129
Oh, my God.
You gave me tea.

692
00:36:22,338 --> 00:36:25,132
- Yes.
- How did you know?

693
00:36:25,800 --> 00:36:27,009
It's perfectly obvious.

694
00:36:27,468 --> 00:36:29,970
I also know who the father is
but don't... don't worry.

695
00:36:30,221 --> 00:36:31,430
Your secret is safe with me.

696
00:36:31,639 --> 00:36:35,059
Lisbon. Perfect timing.
Just in time to open your present.

697
00:36:35,601 --> 00:36:37,353
- What's going on?
- I spiked the coffee.

698
00:36:37,520 --> 00:36:43,025
Somebody in this room
is about to spiral into a rapid detox.

699
00:36:43,526 --> 00:36:46,112
The shakes, nausea
those dreaded cravings

700
00:36:46,278 --> 00:36:48,906
for the rush of a fresh hit...

701
00:36:49,824 --> 00:36:52,993
- Hello. Someone's missing.
- I don't see Dr. Gidry.

702
00:36:54,704 --> 00:36:57,707
The anesthesiologist.
Of course.

703
00:36:59,333 --> 00:37:00,376
Lisbon. Hurry.

704
00:37:05,005 --> 00:37:06,048
Drop the needle!

705
00:37:06,549 --> 00:37:10,177
No, no, you... you... you don't
understand. I, uh, I need this.

706
00:37:10,720 --> 00:37:13,139
- I'm going through withdrawal.
- No, you're not.

707
00:37:14,557 --> 00:37:15,599
But the coffee...

708
00:37:15,725 --> 00:37:17,727
Jane didn't put anything
in the coffee.

709
00:37:18,644 --> 00:37:21,063
He needed to lure out the real killer,
and here you are.

710
00:37:28,154 --> 00:37:30,781
Okay, okay. I-I-I admit it.

711
00:37:30,906 --> 00:37:34,785
I-I-I stole drugs and I returned
them watered down, but...

712
00:37:35,911 --> 00:37:37,246
That doesn't make me the killer.

713
00:37:39,999 --> 00:37:42,334
Can we... can we just get...
get a little fresh air in here?

714
00:37:42,460 --> 00:37:43,836
It's stifling.

715
00:37:44,003 --> 00:37:45,212
Tell me how you started using.

716
00:37:47,298 --> 00:37:48,340
Residency?

717
00:37:50,217 --> 00:37:51,761
Up days at a time.

718
00:37:52,094 --> 00:37:54,555
I mean how else were you supposed to
stay alert enough to perform?

719
00:37:56,223 --> 00:38:02,062
And then I'd... I'd need something else
to help me come... come back... down.

720
00:38:02,521 --> 00:38:04,148
And when did Newton figure out
you had a problem?

721
00:38:04,899 --> 00:38:07,818
I don't have a problem!
I maintain perfectly!

722
00:38:08,944 --> 00:38:11,906
No. Your real withdrawals
are starting.

723
00:38:12,907 --> 00:38:15,034
You work with me here,
and I can get you what you need?

724
00:38:22,541 --> 00:38:23,584
Last week...

725
00:38:27,505 --> 00:38:30,132
Newton was doing
a review of O.R. cases

726
00:38:30,549 --> 00:38:33,886
and he found some inconsistencies
in patient care.

727
00:38:34,929 --> 00:38:35,971
So he brought you in.

728
00:38:36,764 --> 00:38:40,142
He said that my actions had...

729
00:38:41,727 --> 00:38:44,814
had left the hospital
exposed to lawsuits.

730
00:38:44,980 --> 00:38:49,235
Zero tolerance means zero tolerance.
Blah, blah, blah...

731
00:38:50,277 --> 00:38:51,320
So he fired you?

732
00:38:51,445 --> 00:38:54,198
No, no, no, not just... not just
fire me, no. He... he was gonna...

733
00:38:54,323 --> 00:38:57,076
He was gonna report me to the state
medical board. Huh?

734
00:38:57,451 --> 00:38:59,286
And cooperate
with the police if asked.

735
00:38:59,411 --> 00:39:01,831
He called it moral obligation.
I called it covering his ass.

736
00:39:02,915 --> 00:39:04,250
So...

737
00:39:06,377 --> 00:39:08,003
I tried to reason with him.

738
00:39:09,755 --> 00:39:11,715
"After his lecture, you followed him
to the driving range."

739
00:39:12,341 --> 00:39:13,384
I'm sorry.

740
00:39:13,509 --> 00:39:15,135
"He said he was sorry,
but he just kept swinging."

741
00:39:15,427 --> 00:39:18,305
"He was gonna destroy everything
that I'd worked for"

742
00:39:18,430 --> 00:39:22,017
"but he kept on swinging,
and I lost it."

743
00:39:27,565 --> 00:39:28,607
You killed him.

744
00:39:30,484 --> 00:39:32,820
My life didn't matter to him.

745
00:39:34,029 --> 00:39:36,407
Why should his matter to me?

746
00:39:40,661 --> 00:39:41,954
So...

747
00:39:43,914 --> 00:39:47,167
- Are you gonna help me out?
- No.

748
00:39:54,300 --> 00:39:55,342
Got Gidry's confession.

749
00:39:55,467 --> 00:39:56,844
Golenka's being deported tomorrow.

750
00:39:57,052 --> 00:39:59,305
He'll be back just in time to greet Oratni
and his pre-owned kidney.

751
00:39:59,430 --> 00:40:02,725
Now that quick's been fired for trading
an M.R.I. machine for a kidney

752
00:40:02,850 --> 00:40:05,895
let's hope the hospital's transplant
program stays on the up-and-up.

753
00:40:06,103 --> 00:40:08,188
Yeah, there's an endless supply of doctors
like quick in the world.

754
00:40:08,480 --> 00:40:10,649
- Way to see the bright side.
- Need anything else?

755
00:40:12,443 --> 00:40:16,947
I want you to know that my reinstatement
is in no way a reflection of your abilities.

756
00:40:17,740 --> 00:40:19,700
- You did a great job.
- I know.

757
00:40:20,284 --> 00:40:21,327
Hey, guys. Come on in.

758
00:40:26,540 --> 00:40:28,375
So we have a question.

759
00:40:29,501 --> 00:40:32,630
If there's a group hug coming,
I am so outta here.

760
00:40:32,755 --> 00:40:33,797
No hugs.

761
00:40:33,923 --> 00:40:36,008
We're going out for a drink
to celebrate the return of Cho.

762
00:40:36,258 --> 00:40:37,301
You want to join us?

763
00:40:38,928 --> 00:40:40,721
Guys, thank you. I can't.

764
00:40:41,138 --> 00:40:43,682
I got a lot of paperwork to do
and there's a management meeting.

765
00:40:44,683 --> 00:40:46,393
- Next time.
- Right.

766
00:40:46,518 --> 00:40:47,686
- Good night.
- Next time.

767
00:40:48,562 --> 00:40:49,897
- Good night.
- Night, boss.

768
00:40:54,652 --> 00:40:56,028
The price of power.

769
00:41:00,032 --> 00:41:02,201
Patrick. There you are.

770
00:41:03,452 --> 00:41:06,538
Yep. Here I am.
You caught me.

771
00:41:06,914 --> 00:41:09,458
Yeah. I, I didn't want to take up
too much of your time, uh...

772
00:41:09,583 --> 00:41:12,294
I, I just wanted to let you know
that they found a kidney for Enid.

773
00:41:13,545 --> 00:41:14,797
They're operating tonight.

774
00:41:15,130 --> 00:41:16,757
I think your advocacy
had a lot to do with that.

775
00:41:16,882 --> 00:41:20,886
Oh, no, no. Good for Enid.
It's... Good luck with that.

776
00:41:21,804 --> 00:41:23,013
I wanted to give you this.

777
00:41:26,266 --> 00:41:28,811
St. Sebastian.
Gave me a lot of strength.

778
00:41:30,354 --> 00:41:31,438
Maybe he'll do the same for you.

779
00:41:31,814 --> 00:41:34,024
A magical medallion.
That's... that's cool.

780
00:41:35,985 --> 00:41:37,486
He helps people in pain.

781
00:41:38,821 --> 00:41:39,863
But, uh...

782
00:41:41,699 --> 00:41:43,867
You know, seriously, I'm...
I'm not really a believer.

783
00:41:48,539 --> 00:41:51,750
You know what? Never mind.
Thank you very much.
